WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.760
- Welcome back y'all I'm hanging
out with Cassandra Freeman.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:03.878
Give it up.

00:00:03.878 --> 00:00:05.241
(audience cheering)

00:00:05.241 --> 00:00:06.750
Who's jamming with the band.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:09.990
Earlier this spring, the
Forbes 30/50 Summit convened

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:10.980
in Abu Dhabi.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.110
The event featured some
of the most powerful

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.150
and innovative women in the world.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:16.830
Attendees included Hillary Clinton,

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.290
Nobel Prize winner Malala Yousafzai,

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.600
Misty Copeland, and Gloria Steinem,

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.120
it's an incredible amount of
people, just to name a few.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.760
And the whole thing was
chaired by journalist

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.610
and Know Your Value
founder Mika Brzezinski.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:31.620
Just before the summit here on the show,

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:34.050
Mika surprised two female entrepreneurs

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.540
with tickets to a once
in a lifetime event,

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.040
y'all gotta check this out.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.990
- I would love to invite you both,

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:43.890
I will give you tickets to be
my guest at the 30/50 Summit

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:47.520
in Abu Dhabi, share ideas
and to help lift women up

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:48.450
from around the world.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.564
Will you come with me?
(audience applauds)

00:00:49.564 --> 00:00:51.489
- Its so cool.

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:52.447
- Thank you Mika.

00:00:52.447 --> 00:00:53.660
- That's so cool.
- Thank you.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:54.660
- Thank you.

00:00:55.572 --> 00:00:57.990
- I am so stoked to find out how it went,

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.940
so dialed in from New York, please welcome

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:02.550
the co-host of Morning
Joe, Mika Brzezinski,

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.980
as well as the founders
of Vontelle Eyewear,

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.720
Tracy and Nancy here in the studio.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:07.780
Give it up!

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:09.452
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:01:09.452 --> 00:01:12.330
(upbeat music)

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.400
Oh my gosh, so first of all,

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.470
Mika, Cassandra, everybody, hey!

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:17.700
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.800
And Mika I'm gonna start with you.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:23.910
You were host to the most
powerful women on the planet,

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:24.870
have you recovered?

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:26.370
Was alcohol involved?

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.383
I feel very nervous about that.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.650
- Afterwards, no, it was incredible.

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:33.870
It surpassed all expectations.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.390
It was inspirational, aspirational,

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:40.260
and every woman who attended
knew that growing their value,

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.780
they left there knowing it was possible

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:44.820
and with things to do for themselves.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:49.820
We had over 50 different
countries represented, 500 women.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.370
And my gosh, this setting was
like the Louvre, the palace.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:57.090
We had a party in the desert,
and you had Catherine O'Hara,

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.640
and Ayesha Curry and Jessica Alba,

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.740
and then this incredible, Misty Copeland,

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:05.610
this incredible panel
with Billy Jean King,

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.920
Gloria Steinem, Olena Zelenska,

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.690
and then my co-host

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:11.490
was Hillary Rodham Clinton.
(audience applauds)

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:13.650
So, it was unbelievable.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:16.410
And as you can see in some of the photos,

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:19.650
we had an award ceremony at
the Louvre on that stage.

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:21.780
Tracy and Nancy and I got on the stage

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.090
after the award ceremony in the moonlight

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:27.180
and we had our selfie moment (laughs)

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:31.200
to really connect and we just
hugged and we were jumping

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.300
up and down and going around in circles

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.580
'cause we were so excited

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.500
about how this event had turned out.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.600
It was remarkable.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.230
- I can't even imagine the energy of just,

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:45.720
you just mentioned so
many powerful people,

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:46.680
like powerful women,

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:49.410
like the energy in that
room must have been,

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:52.470
I mean you could have
got drunk off that alone,

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:55.350
you know, it's just such a
powerful thing to be a part of.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:57.510
Tracy and Nancy remind
everybody the challenges

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.190
that your business is facing.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:01.320
- Well we're both from Corporate America,

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.690
and we had no experience
in the eyewear business

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:05.400
when we launched our company.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.980
And now we have, our sales are growing,

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:10.560
we have a great partnership
with Nickelodeon,

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.780
but we still need investment
dollars to scale our business

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.190
in order to get it to the next level.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.023
- Absolutely.
- Yeah,

00:03:15.023 --> 00:03:17.220
and the whole thing we were excited

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:20.250
and thrilled to be invited to the event,

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:23.160
and our goal was to meet
women who could help us

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:26.070
scale and get to the next
level of our business.

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.980
- Wow, what a room to network in. (laughs)

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:29.820
That's crazy.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:31.680
So Tracy and Nancy were kind enough

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.380
to document their entire
journey to Abu Dhabi.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.880
So let's check out what
their experience was like.

00:03:37.966 --> 00:03:38.799
(gentle music)

00:03:38.799 --> 00:03:41.460
- Pack in the car heading to Abu Dhabi.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:44.850
We are going to rub shoulders
with Hillary Clinton,

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:49.020
Misty Copeland, Jessica
Alba, Ayesha Curry.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:51.660
Looking forward to meeting
all of the fabulous women.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:52.767
- What's up!

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:55.830
- Thank you to the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:59.400
for hooking us up with
the Forbes 30/50 Summit

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.800
hosted by Mika Brzezinski.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:02.633
We made it.

00:04:02.633 --> 00:04:04.527
Welcome to Abu Dhabi.

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:08.880
- Just landed, it's 2:30 New York time,

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:12.750
but it's like 10:45 in the morning here.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:13.923
Are you excited?

00:04:13.923 --> 00:04:16.500
- Super excited and super exhausted.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:18.670
- She's loud for early in the morning.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:20.130
(upbeat music)

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:20.963
We have arrived.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:26.262
Oh my goodness, look at
this room, it's beautiful.

00:04:26.262 --> 00:04:28.198
(water whooshing)

00:04:28.198 --> 00:04:29.340
It's beautiful.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:30.960
The sun is going down.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:35.347
- Today is the official day.

00:04:35.347 --> 00:04:37.170
- I can't contain my excitement.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.280
- We are trying.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:40.410
- Hello to everybody from everyone here

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:42.965
at the 30/50 Summit in Abu Dhabi.

00:04:42.965 --> 00:04:44.130
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:45.450
We're having a great time.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:48.780
- I'm so thankful for this conference.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:50.520
- The more powerful you are,

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:52.290
the faster you can make things happen.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:55.680
- We're making slow but steady progress

00:04:55.680 --> 00:05:00.680
on a range of issues that
affect women and girls.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:03.060
- What really inspires
me is that previously

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:05.850
it was thought that first
ladies are just soft power,

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:08.190
but we have showed that it
is not just a formality,

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:10.705
we're not just a soft
force, we are a force.

00:05:10.705 --> 00:05:12.685
(audience applauding)

00:05:12.685 --> 00:05:14.400
- I was very excited, you
know, that I would be here.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.147
I saw you on the Kelly
Clarkson Show and I was like,

00:05:16.147 --> 00:05:18.060
"Oh my God!"

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.520
The rest of the day is gonna be amazing.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.230
The gala tonight is gonna be great

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:24.577
and it's just so great
to see you all in person.

00:05:24.577 --> 00:05:27.937
(camera clicking)

00:05:27.937 --> 00:05:29.337
- I'm so proud you guys came.

00:05:29.337 --> 00:05:30.755
- All because of you,

00:05:30.755 --> 00:05:31.620
all because you.
- Oh, we love you,

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:33.416
you're amazing.
- So fun.

00:05:33.416 --> 00:05:34.488
- Thank you for having us.

00:05:34.488 --> 00:05:35.558
- Thank you for coming.

00:05:35.558 --> 00:05:36.391
- Thank you for doing this for us,

00:05:36.391 --> 00:05:38.070
you dunno how much we've been networking.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.560
- Good, look at this room, turn it around.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:42.090
Look at this, ooh.

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:44.783
- Mika Brzezinski, you don't
know what you've done for us.

00:05:44.783 --> 00:05:46.470
This is an honor,

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.810
all these beautiful,
smart intelligent women.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:49.920
- All in one room.

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:50.753
- All in one room.

00:05:50.753 --> 00:05:52.503
It's amazing, it's just amazing.

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:56.165
(audience applauds and cheers)
- Oh my gosh.

00:05:56.165 --> 00:05:56.998
Wow!

00:05:58.028 --> 00:05:59.970
That's some serious female power.

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:00.900
I wanna go to that event.

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:01.817
- That is the proof.

00:06:01.817 --> 00:06:04.260
But it just proves like...

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.940
It has to happen in collaboration,

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.470
you have to be put in the room

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:08.790
for those collaborations to happen.

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:11.070
So it's remarkable, remarkable.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:13.140
- So Tracy and Nancy, were either of you

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:14.160
intimidated at first?

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:15.720
'Cause it's a very powerful room,

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:18.870
but they also seem like
people that are very warm

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:20.130
and kind of welcoming and friendly.

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:21.000
So was it good?

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.370
- Yeah, not intimidated,
but very excited to be

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:26.760
at this most lavish conference
in the whole wide world.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:29.940
I mean women from every
country, from every background.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:31.860
And everyone was just so nice to us.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:35.760
You know, we were like excited,
like we snuck into a party,

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:37.237
but after a while people were like,

00:06:37.237 --> 00:06:39.270
"we know you, you're the glasses ladies,

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:40.980
you were on the Kelly Clarkson Show."

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:41.813
- [Kelly] Oh, that's awesome.

00:06:41.813 --> 00:06:43.980
- And that made us feel just amazing,

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:45.930
and we realized that everyone

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:47.520
just had a great story to tell.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:49.860
And everyone wanted to
help us and talk to us.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:51.840
- Where do you find these glasses from?

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:52.680
Like where do you get them?

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:53.880
Like where do I buy it?
- We create them,

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.140
we create them.
- This is us.

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:56.880
- But like, where do I go buy this?

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:57.870
- Vontelle.com.

00:06:57.870 --> 00:06:59.144
- There you go, vontelle.com.

00:06:59.144 --> 00:07:00.150
(audience applauds)

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:00.983
What about you?

00:07:00.983 --> 00:07:02.700
Like how was your experience?

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:04.650
- So as Tracy said, not intimidating,

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:08.220
but we got to meet women
from every walk of life.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:10.890
And we found that we
all had common ground,

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:13.740
we all had a mission, for
us, it was the eyeglasses.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:16.170
So we created Vontelle,
but we met women who were

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:19.620
software engineers, bankers, attorneys,

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.020
mortgage brokers who
decided that they were going

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:24.630
to start over and create
their own business.

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:26.040
They created their own lane.

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:28.110
So, that just goes to show you that,

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:29.700
you know, you think that you're different,

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:31.170
you come from all different walks of life.

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:33.990
We're talking about women
who came from 50 countries

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:35.100
around the world,

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.380
but we all had that common ground

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:40.170
that we saw a need and
we decided to fill it,

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:41.970
if not us, then who?

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:45.090
- Yeah, so Mika, a big part
of the summit was mentorship.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:46.620
So tell us about that.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.660
- Well that's what it's all about.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:50.550
And my gosh, I couldn't have put it better

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:53.370
than Tracy and Nancy in terms
of the experience in itself,

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:57.540
but we have an app, we
had networking sessions,

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:00.090
mentoring sessions, and you know,

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:02.947
it sounds kind of like
networking, kind of like,

00:08:02.947 --> 00:08:05.340
"oh, I gotta network today" is sort of how

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:06.960
some younger women feel like.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:09.180
It's just kind of challenging and scary.

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:11.910
We pulled it off, not only
do we know how to party,

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:14.610
we know how to network and connect.

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:17.280
And you really came away
with a lot of key messages.

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:20.070
Number 1, it's about the
money and that is okay,

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:23.430
number 2, how to know your
value, what is that about?

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:25.170
How to communicate it effectively?

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:27.990
And lastly, no matter what,

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:29.760
you have a much longer runway

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:31.470
than you ever imagined in your life,

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:35.370
so you have time to
slow down, do it right,

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:38.700
fall down, get up, start over again.

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:40.200
You got lots of time.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:41.272
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:08:41.272 --> 00:08:42.780
(audience applauding)

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:45.660
So Sandra, like mentorship
is a huge thing.

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:47.340
It's a huge thing in your life too, right?

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:48.173
Mentorship?
- No, for sure.

00:08:48.173 --> 00:08:49.590
First of all, Mika, you can have a church

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.330
of just the amen of like what it means

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:52.410
to bring people together.

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:53.700
I so believe in all of that,

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:55.770
and you know, I was a
professor for 12 years

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:58.020
in New York City at Fordham University,

00:08:58.020 --> 00:08:59.790
Pace University, and other universities.

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:02.070
So I've always had to mentor people,

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:03.480
but even through creativity,

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.400
we have a whole lane just
for emerging artists.

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:06.780
And what's interesting is that

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:08.910
people who are at the top of their career,

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:11.550
they long to actually mentor people

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:12.750
to bring them in as well.

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:14.610
And especially when you think about like

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:17.940
my show, the creator of our
show is a guy from Kansas City.

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:19.650
He had nothing to do with California.

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:21.547
So, thankfully someone
like Will Smith was like,

00:09:21.547 --> 00:09:24.600
"yes, we love this idea,
come to LA, let's do it."

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:26.340
We need more mentorship to happen.

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:29.370
- Cassandra, I'm curious
what are you doing

00:09:29.370 --> 00:09:31.560
on International Women's Day next year?

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:34.980
This is an annual event, we
would love to honor you there.

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:36.840
And Kelly,

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:37.710
hello?

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:38.850
- Oh, what?
- Can you?

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:41.039
- Cassandra and I will show up. (laughs)

00:09:41.039 --> 00:09:43.750
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:45.210
- Okay, that's all you have to say,

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:46.860
where you having it next year honey?

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:47.910
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:48.811
- We'll go wherever you tell us.

00:09:48.811 --> 00:09:50.940
- I was like, first of all,
I've never been to Abu Dhabi.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:52.470
Yeah, I was gonna make that joke

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:53.400
but I was like, "be serious,"

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:54.600
but I'm gonna make the joke now.

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:56.820
I mean, seriously, you picked
such a stinker of a place

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:57.653
to throw a party. (laughs)

00:09:57.653 --> 00:10:00.180
I was like, that place looks gorgeous.

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:03.060
Like it just sets up the environment.

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:04.890
- They might have seen
me dancing in the desert

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:06.900
very late at night with a hundred women,

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:09.000
but maybe not, but probably.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.580
